  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "d4c40a7b-f616-4ba5-bd72-64622d767cca",
      "name": "Overview Sticky",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -700,
        -60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 840,
        "content": "## Lead notification and auto-reply\nReceives a new lead through a secured webhook, alerts your team by email, sends the lead an acknowledgement and logs everything.\n\n### How it works\n1. A form or CRM sends the lead to the webhook (Header Auth protected).\n2. Fields are cleaned and validated; invalid payloads get a 400 response.\n3. A Data Table lookup skips leads that were already notified.\n4. Two Gmail emails go out in parallel: an admin alert and a lead acknowledgement.\n5. Both results are merged, logged in the Data Table and returned to the caller.\n\n### Setup steps\n1. Create a Header Auth credential and select it on the webhook.\n2. Connect a Gmail OAuth2 credential on both Gmail nodes.\n3. Create a Data Table named `lead_notification_log` with string columns: leadId, executionId, adminEmailStatus, adminEmailError, leadEmailStatus, leadEmailError, status, notifiedAt. Select it in both Data Table nodes.\n4. Replace `admin@example.com` in the admin email node.\n5. Test with a POST of `{leadId, name, email, company, service, message}`, then activate.\n\n### Customization tips\n- Edit the acknowledgement text to match your brand.\n- Set an Error Workflow in the workflow settings."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
